What I Learned

Through this learning experience, I studied fundamental networking concepts, including:

OSI Model: The seven layers used to understand network communication.
TCP/IP: The protocol suite that enables devices to communicate across networks.
IP Addresses: How devices are logically identified on a network.
MAC Addresses: Hardware-level addressing used for communication on local networks.
Ports and Protocols: How network services communicate using protocols and port numbers.
Network Devices: The roles of switches and routers in connecting devices and networks.
Network Troubleshooting: Understanding networking concepts that help identify connectivity issues.
